{
 "rule": "Part II independent-read reference. PRIMARY on all four human datasets: biological-replicate split with EXPECTED-depth matching (per transcript the deeper replicate is binomially thinned with p = shallower total / deeper total; realised totals vary and are recorded). Both role assignments (rep1\u2192input/rep2\u2192reference and the swap) are run; the deeper replicate is not treated as truth. SENSITIVITY: binomial read-level partition of pooled counts, only on the three UMI-deduplicated datasets; not on GSE133393. Every Part II result must report, per dataset and depth bin, N_eligible (in T_low), N_with_reference (shallower replicate > 0) and N_scored (correlations defined after thinning); undefined correlations are never scored as 0 and results on the scored subset are not extrapolated to all of T_low.",
 "wording": "A pooled binomial split overestimates the agreement between independent libraries; for GSE133393 (no deduplication possible) the overestimate is large. The comparison does not apportion the gap between PCR duplication and library-to-library/biological variation.",
